-- PAPER-LEARN-SETTLE-E-1 (2026-11-05, charter pillar autonomy; GitHub QNFO/qnfo-workers#5788, #5795, #6154; agent_issues 1000871, 1000920, 1000975; cluster E-metrics-portfolio).
-- The three PAPER-LEARN-1 issues close when no direct learning of their paper version is still `proposed` (their contract probes count exactly that). Twelve direct learnings were read in full
-- against the live fleet on 2026-11-05 (claim, lever, application and the model's apply signal) and each given one disposition with its reason: one is applied (the pull request that carries this file),
-- seven are already in place (the mechanism is named and was read today), four are rejected (a category, the specific reason, and what would justify proposing again).
-- The model's apply signal ("no listed mechanism") came from a catalogue of six mechanisms; it usually meant the model did not know the fleet already does this (the same finding as PAPER-LEARN-PROBATION-SETTLE-1).
-- Revert one row: UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'proposed' WHERE id = <id>.
-- APPLY-BY: ci
-- DB: qnfo-audit
-- Rollback: UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = (SELECT b.fleet_status FROM bak_20261105_e_pl_settle b WHERE b.id = paper_learnings.id), status_note = (SELECT b.status_note FROM bak_20261105_e_pl_settle b WHERE b.id = paper_learnings.id), updated_at = (SELECT b.updated_at FROM bak_20261105_e_pl_settle b WHERE b.id = paper_learnings.id) WHERE id IN (SELECT id FROM bak_20261105_e_pl_settle)

CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS bak_20261105_e_pl_settle AS SELECT id, fleet_status, status_note, updated_at FROM paper_learnings WHERE id IN (5672, 5673, 5675, 5676, 5677, 5678, 5679, 5683, 5734, 5735, 5736, 5737);

-- recursive-self-consistency 2.0.0 (issue 1000871)
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'already-in-place', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 in place (E-metrics-portfolio session, 2026-11-05; sourcing): A claim attributed to a source is checked against that source before it is published: CITE-FULLTEXT-1 and SOURCE-VOICE-1 make every generator that writes about another work ground it on the full text and drop a work it cannot read, VERIFY-ZERO-CLAIMS-1 (qnfo-research-exec 0.29.0) logs a paper whose claim extraction finds nothing, and the reference-existence gate is in flight as RM-CITE-EXISTENCE-GATE-1 (roadmap 1691). Errata per sourced claim are the outcome measures papers_with_open_high_errata_pct (1.5 on 2026-11-05) and errata_high_net_inflow_7d. A code diff cites sources rarely; REVIEW-GATE-1 already requires an evidence line that is an added line of the diff.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 5672 AND fleet_status = 'proposed';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'rejected', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 rejected (E-metrics-portfolio session, 2026-11-05; no-measured-gap): Remediation scope is narrow by construction: a code-task edits one verbatim code-anchor that occurs once in one file, cmScope denies paths the loop may not change, and REVIEW-GATE-1 reads a risky diff with two model families. No merged code-task pull request is shown whose diff went beyond its anchor, and a blast-radius metric needs per-PR line counts the code_tasks table does not store (it holds the branch, the pull request URL and the merge SHA). Re-propose with a merged code-task PR that changed unrelated code.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 5673 AND fleet_status = 'proposed';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'already-in-place', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 in place (E-metrics-portfolio session, 2026-11-05; clusters): Selective partial remediation of a related set is visible per family: v_issue_family_throughput lists, per issue family, opened, closed, open now, net inflow and drain ratio (ISSUE-THROUGHPUT-1), closure_branching_ratio_24h (0.337 on 2026-11-05) measures closes that spawn new issues, and issue_lifecycle records every open and close, so a family with closed members and open siblings is a row with open_now above 0 and closes in the window. Each defect is its own agent_issues row with its own contract probe (ORPHAN-GUARD-BIRTH-1).', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 5675 AND fleet_status = 'proposed';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'already-in-place', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 in place (E-metrics-portfolio session, 2026-11-05; closure-wording): A metric closure states the measurement against the bound, not a verdict: close_evidence is written as the value against the trigger threshold (for example "cf_agent_requests_over_120m=0" against a trigger of greater than 0), a contract probe distinguishes `recovering` from `1`, and RELAPSE-HOLD-1 (v_issue_close_hold, migration_runs 1149) holds a closing pass for 20 to 120 minutes until the passes since the last reopen span the hold. The reading of v_relapse_6h_cohort (relapse within 6 hours of a close 0.310 before the hold, 0.085 after, 2026-11-05) measures false-confidence closures directly.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 5676 AND fleet_status = 'proposed';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'applied', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 applied (E-metrics-portfolio session, 2026-11-05; sweep): the learning is undercorrection, fixing one occurrence of a defect without sweeping for the others. Measured case: the D1 limit on a LIKE or GLOB pattern (50 bytes, the statement errors on every run) was fixed one file at a time on 2026-10-13 (migrations/2026-10-13-08-probe-like-limit.sql) and again on 2026-11-04 in cron-watch (PR 7277), the blind-spot audit (PR 7281) and the closing probe of issue 1001342 (PR 7282), plus the case-insensitive match PR 7283 had to restore. scripts/d1_like_limit_guard.py (D1-LIKE-LIMIT-GUARD-1) is the sweep that stays: diff-only, it fails a change that adds a LIKE or GLOB literal over 50 bytes (replayed on commit 620b196d it flags the two BLINDSPOT-1 patterns), run by scripts/pr_fast_guards.py on every change; suite scripts/d1-like-limit-guard.test.mjs. This migration ships in that pull request.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 5677 AND fleet_status = 'proposed';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'rejected', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 rejected (E-metrics-portfolio session, 2026-11-05; no-measured-gap): A fleet-computed limit already records its derivation: metric_registry requires a formula and a source_of_truth per metric, analytics_metric_triggers carries the threshold with its notes, and PAPER-LEARN-PROJECTIONS-1 (qnfo-lifecycle 1.17.6) labels generated derived and assumption outputs as model projections, not measured facts. The one measured stale limit (the compiled RESEARCH_DAILY_NEURONS_DEFAULT shadowed by ops_config research_daily_neurons, issue 1000988) is a precedence defect, not a missing sensitivity record. Re-propose with a threshold that went stale because an input assumption changed and a recorded sensitivity would have flagged it.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 5678 AND fleet_status = 'proposed';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'rejected', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 rejected (E-metrics-portfolio session, 2026-11-05; no-measured-gap): A disconfirmation of the fleet''s own prior output is already kept and credited, not discarded: a prediction that did not match is logged with outcome_matched (prediction_miss_rate_7d 0.254 on 2026-11-05, so misses are retained and scored), every change to a paper, retraction and withdrawal is an immutable paper_change_ledger row (PAPER-LEDGER-1), and q08_retraction_rate_30d is an outcome measure the desk is graded on. No run is shown that was counted failed because it disconfirmed an earlier output. Re-propose with such a run.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 5679 AND fleet_status = 'proposed';

-- number-systems-as-stratified-distinction-operations-an-enclosure-hierarchy-over- 3.0.0 (issue 1000920)
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'already-in-place', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 in place (E-metrics-portfolio session, 2026-11-05; validity): A count that is definitional rather than informative is what a validity measure is for: output_quality_measures carries role `validity` rows (paper_new_score_saturation_14d, 0.672 on 2026-11-05; golden_run_complement_share_30d; q08_panel_effective_votes_30d; outreach_engaged_per_100_clicks_7d) and role `proxy` rows that never count toward a verdict, and OUTPUT-QUALITY-LEDGER-1 treats a measure that cannot move any more as a validity finding. READER-YIELD-1 applies it to clicks (a floor of automated visits), which is why readers are read from engaged sessions.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 5683 AND fleet_status = 'proposed';

-- paper-beyond-the-qubit 3.0.0 (issue 1000975)
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'already-in-place', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 in place (E-metrics-portfolio session, 2026-11-05; retract): A quantitative claim with no source is removed, not re-estimated, in the two places the fleet publishes numbers: the q08 desk checks the names, years and figures of a draft against its source material (groundPreCheck, Q08-FACT-LEDGER-1, q08-signal-engine 0.32.0) and prunes an unsupported sentence or ends the run instead of softening it, and a published paper carries an erratum and a revision, never a silent change (PAPER-LEDGER-1, immutable change rows). CITE-FULLTEXT-1 grounds every cited work on its full text.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 5734 AND fleet_status = 'proposed';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'rejected', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 rejected (E-metrics-portfolio session, 2026-11-05; infeasible-check): Tagging every number as derived, cited or assumption needs a reader that decides which sentences are numeric claims and whether the arithmetic shown reproduces them; a deterministic gate cannot, and a model judge adds a correlated layer that ENSEMBLE-POLICY-1 tells the pipeline to keep few. The numeric checks that exist are deterministic or source-grounded: VERIFY-ZERO-CLAIMS-1 (a paper with 6 or more numeric equalities and no extracted claim), the q08 source-grounding stage and PAPER-LEARN-PROJECTIONS-1 for generated outputs. Re-propose with a published paper whose untagged number produced an erratum that a tag would have prevented.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 5735 AND fleet_status = 'proposed';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'already-in-place', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 in place (E-metrics-portfolio session, 2026-11-05; falsify): A standing claim the fleet acts on carries the observation that would refute it: belief_registry holds each belief with a `belief-<key>` probe that fails when the belief is false (DOCTRINE-1), every issue is born with its closing probe (ORPHAN-GUARD-BIRTH-1) which states in advance what observation closes it, and every autonomous decision names its rollback_path and predicted_outcome in decision_log.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 5736 AND fleet_status = 'proposed';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'already-in-place', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 in place (E-metrics-portfolio session, 2026-11-05; band): A budget rule is applied inside the band it was fit in: v_research_volume_target (READER-YIELD-1) sets the research budget from 28 days of engaged-reader data, moves at most 10 percent a day and clamps to a stated floor (180000) and ceiling (450000) neurons, and the governor pauses on any other writer of the key; fleet_budget caps steer models and never stop work (BUDGET-SOFT-ROUTE-1).', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 5737 AND fleet_status = 'proposed';
